The fused mHC readout and RMS normalization kernel in
models/cuda/resin_models_cuda/glm5_3_flash/mhc_cuda.py is adapted from SGLang,
revision baa9befa381511cd4d56f83980951e5a45fffc6d,
python/sglang/kernels/ops/layernorm/mhc.py.
https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/baa9befa381511cd4d56f83980951e5a45fffc6d/python/sglang/kernels/ops/layernorm/mhc.py
SGLang is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The adaptation keeps
token count dynamic, uses a fixed reduction split, and disables PDL scheduling.

The accepted-prefix KDA state kernel in
models/cuda/resin_models_cuda/glm5_3_flash/kda_state_cuda.py is adapted from
flash-linear-attention 0.5.2, fla/ops/kda/fused_recurrent.py.
https://github.com/fla-org/flash-linear-attention/blob/v0.5.2/fla/ops/kda/fused_recurrent.py
The MIT license and copyright notice are retained at
models/cuda/resin_models_cuda/glm5_3_flash/LICENSE.fla. The adaptation computes
only accepted recurrent state, with Resin's FP32 beta sigmoid and explicit
preservation of empty rows; it does not produce attention outputs.

